  "slug": "aav-guided-0537",
  "summary": "Deep learning models trained on simulated or self-supervised data now target low-SNR, aberrated, and cryo-ET imaging limits.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is machine learning applied to microscopy data where acquisition quality or missing ground truth limits analysis. TomoSegNet trains a cryo-electron tomography membrane segmentation model solely on data simulated from a biophysical membrane model. A self-supervised neural field jointly estimates spatially variant optical aberrations and reconstructs 3D structure from a single blurred image. A paired high/low-SNR fluorescence dataset of 324 images across 12 sub-datasets benchmarks three deep denoising models and a tile-stitching approach for extreme low-SNR restoration. The Cell Behavior Video Classification Challenge separately benchmarks 35 computer vision methods on time-lapse videos, comparing tracking-based features with end-to-end deep models. What is new is the reliance on simulation and self-supervision to supply training signal in place of experimental annotation, alongside standardized benchmarking of competing approaches.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-20"
}
